\ ==== unterminated quotation ====

\ An unterminated quotation inside a definition (a [: / [: with no
\ matching :]) must fail loudly and discard the half-built word, not segfault.
\ The system must recover and keep compiling/running normally afterward.

: bad [: 1 2 ;
bad
: bad2 [: a b | a ;
bad2
1 2 + .
: good 6 7 + ;
good .
[ 1 2 3 ] [: dup * :] map .
cr

clear

\ ==== partial definition rollback ====

\ a definition that fails mid-compile rolls back entirely: no callable stub
: loopy | acc | [: no-such-word :] ;
loopy

\ compiler state is clean afterward: locals compile and run fine
: fine 3 to a a ;
fine . cr

\ a failing load caught by catch rolls back too
": broken | q | [: no-such-word :] ;" "/tmp/w124_bad.h2o" write-file
[: "/tmp/w124_bad.h2o" load :] catch . cr . cr
broken

\ a definition spanning lines is abandoned by an error on a later line
: partial
nosuchword
partial

clear
